  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "text": "The photos aren't lost, they are 6 yr old photos that are present in the Google Photos Cloud. I restored them to a phone so I may edit them and use them. Restored images are sitting on their original calendar dates instead of the top. How can you expect anyone using a photo editing app or other app to spend time scrolling through 2026 to 2020 images when they have a lot of images? It never used to be like this. Your links are not relevant to the issue. Something changed on the backend. Thanks",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "b83d8437-28ca-4f9d-a453-36dd41556022",
      "date": "2026-09-07",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "forgot_exact_date"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the more section of the app, I can no longer send, print, email, etc. I have tried everything. Every time i download photos from google messages, it doesn't go in the same day I downloaded it. It downloads whatever month or year they took the photo, which is annoying. It takes take me forever to find it. Every update it gets worse. Are you listening to what people are telling you. Stop sending us links to try to fix the problem you caused. That's what you get paid for.",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "37aa9ab3-cd5c-402a-99e1-bd592005552b",
      "date": "2026-07-14",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "forgot_exact_date"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Videos are bugging in my timeline. From a week ago till now, I can't search my backed up videos on Google Photos because as I scroll down my timeline, newer videos appear on wrong dates. This issue doesn't happen on desktop enviroment. I cleared my cache and did a reset on the app, but I'm sure this is a server-side problem. submitted by /u/Nusirra [link] [comments]",
      "source": "Reddit",
      "source_id": "reddit_t3_1fqsvox",
      "date": "2024-09-27",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "forgot_exact_date"
      ],
      "segment": "millennial"
    },
    {
      "text": "I HATE the new organization of Collections. Now I have to click through multiple menus to find my folders, it takes longer and I don't want or need it. I also wish I could default to open on my Device folders which is what I use the most. I do not care about Memories. I hate the pop-ups that constantly ask me to back up my photos (which I do not want to do). This app gets worse and worse with every update. At least allow us to customize our default view! Please!!",
      "source": "Google Play Store",
      "source_id": "3d80bfdb-7b6f-4b5a-9b8c-3a89bb90615d",
      "date": "2024-12-05",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "tags": [
        "forgot_filename_or_album"
      ],
      "segment": "gen_x"
